-- title:
--   Level dictionary for the descent isomorphism φ
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and let $M'\ge 1$ be divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$; assume the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ is contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ for $H=\ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contain a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\xi$, let $K\subseteq k_0((\mathsf q))$ be the $k_0$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the rational function field of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$, $H=\mathrm{levelH}(q\ell)M'$, let $G\le\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K)$ be generated by all $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\xi$ and some $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ — that is, $\mathrm{coeffMap}\,\iota(\tau x)\cdot q\text{-exp}(g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1})=q\text{-exp}(f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1})$ for all integral quotients $x=p_f/p_g$ of weight-$k$ forms on $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ and all $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$ — and let $K_0=K^G$. Then, with $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ a $k_0$-algebra via $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose elements are exactly those all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$, and every $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\simeq F_0$ such that the coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathsf q))$ of each $f\in K_0$ is $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\ell$ (substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{\ell}$) applied to $\varphi f$, the following holds: for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$), every primitive $q\ell$-th root $\xi'\in k_0$ with $\xi'^{\ell}=\zeta$, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K)$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\xi'$ and $\gamma$, the automorphism $\tau$ maps $K_0$ into $K_0$ and $\varphi(\tau f)=\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,(\varphi f)$ for all $f\in K_0$.
--
--   This is the level dictionary underlying the descent from level $q\ell$ to level $q$: it says that an automorphism of the upstairs field read through a primitive $q\ell$-th root $\xi'$ corresponds, under any coefficient-compatible isomorphism $\varphi$ onto the $k_0$-rational part of the level-$q$ component, to the level automorphism of that component attached to $\gamma$ and to the $q$-th root $\zeta=\xi'^{\ell}$, in the style of Shimura's reciprocity laws for automorphisms of modular function fields. It is used in the construction of the framed isomorphism [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_qExpand_framed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_qExpand_framed).
